//! The rust-protobuf approach: stepancheg's `protobuf` v3 runtime (allocating, reflection-
//! capable), generated by `protobuf-codegen`'s pure-Rust parser.
//!
//! Generated messages carry a hidden `special_fields` (so construction uses
//! `..Default::default()`), wrap sub-messages in [`protobuf::MessageField`], and round-trip
//! through `Message::write_to_bytes` / `Message::parse_from_bytes`. The generated types live
//! in [`generated`] (committed, regenerated by `benches/proto-gen`); protobuf-codegen emits
//! one file per `.proto`, so they are stitched into inline modules there.
//!
//! As with the other protobuf approaches, the KLV `u8`/`u16`/`i16` widths widen to
//! `uint32`/`sint32` and the [`flat`] / [`nested`] wrappers narrow back on decode. protobuf
//! has no native framing, so the shared seek-based `encode_framed` / `decode_framed` defaults
//! are inherited (neither overridden). The proto-message construction is inside the timed
//! `encode`, so the bars include the KLV-record -> proto-message map.
//!
//! Author: aav
